  "x-description": "The tree of consequence: the DM's place × time memory as the exact tree it is, from the world down to a focus (default: the busiest region now): world → region → settlement → villages hex (3 km) → houses hex (30 m) → people hex (3 m), with a planet city's society branch (district → crowd → cell → person). Each node: facts_total (memory entries at it or rolled up into it), facts_here, private_facts (counted, never shown), density (per beat, per km²), first/last beat, kinds, newest sample_facts, rolled_up_from (which children rolled up into it) and its latest memory.rollup with the entries it cites. Plus recall paths (a d20's query key → its stored roll → the entry → the roll-ups citing it → the prompts carrying it now; an encounter, an earth event, a settled fact, a person's memory) and totals (entries by scope and kind, ledger rows, persons, observed hexes, the state's bytes by table). Read-only, bounded (at most 2,000 newest entries of each store); `beat`: the memory as it stood then (the society and earth are the live ones).",
  "x-public": true
